s and the the training of the  reads if you look at this picture and  this is something that people working in  next-generation sequencing know very  well is that they a great portion of the  data that you collect from a sequencing  experiment does not belong to the sample  that you're actually interested into and  the reason is that all the technology  that we use the sequencers they all  require a number of adapters primers and  sequences to tag the samples and  barcodes which means that your  sequencing data will contain all these  information that needs to be removed in  order for you to focus on what is  important which is the DNA of your of  your sample removing all this  information is not simple and you  definitely need a bioinformatics which  is able to do that the training step in  the kiya sig panel a plugin workflow is  able to perform automatic trimming which  is capable to recognize and remove also  for example the read-through signal  which might happen for example when the  fragment being sequenced is shorter than  the read length and therefore the  sequence might include a read-through  the reverse complement of the adapter  from the start of the other read the  trimming in these workflow is so  powerful that is able to detect these  read-through even of a single nucleotide  so you understand how accurate your your  analysis becomes when the removal of  these unnecessary information is so  accurate in the beginning and then we  have a very important differential  filtering cascade in the work flow which  is targeted to filter differentially  different type of bearing based on their  size and this is obviously meant to  improve the precision of your result  let's have a look at what kind of  accuracy we can achieve by using these  workflow because all these  characteristics that I just mentioned  they have an effect on your capacity to  obtain very accurate results so in the  tests that we have performed we see very  clearly that we reach a sensitivi